### Configure Resource and Instrumentation Scope for Tracing in Rust

Source: https://context7.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-rust/llms.txt

This Rust code illustrates how to define a `Resource` to identify the service producing telemetry and how to create `InstrumentationScope`s for metadata about the instrumentation library. It shows both simple and scoped tracer initialization, including setting global providers. Ensure `opentelemetry` and `opentelemetry-sdk` are dependencies.

```rust
use opentelemetry::{global, InstrumentationScope, KeyValue};
use opentelemetry::trace::{Tracer, TracerProvider};
use opentelemetry_sdk::trace::SdkTracerProvider;
use opentelemetry_sdk::Resource;

fn main() {
    // Create a resource with service information
    let resource = Resource::builder()
        .with_service_name("order-service")
        .build();

    // Initialize provider with resource
    let provider = SdkTracerProvider::builder()
        .with_resource(resource)
        .build();

    // Method 1: Simple tracer with just a name
    let simple_tracer = provider.tracer("my-library");

    // Method 2: Tracer with full instrumentation scope
    let scope = InstrumentationScope::builder("my-instrumentation-library")
        .with_version(env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION"))
        .with_schema_url("https://opentelemetry.io/schemas/1.17.0")
        .with_attributes(vec![
            KeyValue::new("library.language", "rust"),
            KeyValue::new("library.type", "http-client"),
        ])
        .build();

    let scoped_tracer = provider.tracer_with_scope(scope);

    // Both tracers work the same way
    simple_tracer.in_span("simple_span", |_| {
        println!("Using simple tracer");
    });

    scoped_tracer.in_span("scoped_span", |_| {
        println!("Using scoped tracer with version info");
    });

    // Global access pattern
    global::set_tracer_provider(provider.clone());

    // Get tracer with scope from global
    let global_scope = InstrumentationScope::builder("global-lib")
        .with_version("1.0.0")
        .build();
    let global_tracer = global::tracer_with_scope(global_scope);

    global_tracer.in_span("global_operation", |_| {
        println!("Using global tracer");
    });

    provider.shutdown().expect("Shutdown failed");
}

```

--------------------------------

### Update Tracer Provider Shutdown Pattern

Source: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-rust/blob/main/docs/migration_0.28.md

Demonstrates the migration from the deprecated global shutdown method to explicit tracer provider shutdown in OpenTelemetry Rust 0.28.

```rust
// Before (0.27)
opentelemetry::global::shutdown_tracer_provider();

// After (0.28)
let tracer_provider = opentelemetry_sdk::trace::SdkTracerProvider::builder()
    .build();

// Clone and set the tracer provider globally. Retain the original to invoke shutdown later.
opentelemetry::global::set_tracer_provider(tracer_provider.clone());

// Shutdown the provider when application is exiting.
tracer_provider.shutdown();
```

